    StringEntity(key = "lumea_hair_analysis_report_tip_do_not_miss_spot", value = "Don't miss any spots", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1187),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_treatment_phase_initial_bottomsheet_desc", value = "During the [INITIAL PHASE] which lasts 4 treatments, we schedule your treatment exactly [M/7] weeks after your previous treatment. Perform a treatment within [N] days before or after the planned treatment date during the [INITIAL PHASE].", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1188),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_treatment_phase_touch_up_bottomsheet_desc", value = "<b>Once every 4 weeks</b>\\n\\nAfter the [INITIAL PHASE], use your Lumea once every [X/7] weeks to maintain results. <br> Perform a treatment within [Y] days before or after the planned treatment date during the [TOUCH-UP PHASE].", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1189),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_hair_analysis_tip_no_tattoos_no_private_area", value = "Take a picture of an area where you have no tattoos. Avoid showing private body parts and distinctive personal features (e.g., your face or tattoos) in your photo.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1190),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_imu_discard_feedback_bottomsheet_description_arms", value = "The app is unable to detect the distance between the flashes. To avoid this issue, always: <br><br> \\u2022 Keep skin contact while flashing.<br> \\u2022 Slide the device between flashes.<br> \\u2022 Apply at least 6 flashes in a straight line.<br> \\u2022 Keep your arm still while flashing", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1191),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_imu_movement_body_part_arms", value = "Keep your arm still.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1192),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_imu_results_undetected_instruction_arms", value = "\\u2022 Keep your Lumea in contact with your skin\\n\\u2022 Stop for every flash\\n\\u2022 Apply at least 6 flashes in a straight line\\n\\u2022 Keep your arm still while flashing", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1193),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_expandable_radiance", value = "<b>What does it mean?</b>\\nRadiant skin means your skin is glowing and appears healthy. Radiance is linked to the flow of blood in your skin as well as the way in which light reflects from your skin.\\n\\n<b>What do we measure?</b>\\nTo assess radiant skin, we looked at skin smoothness and skin shine. Strong skin tone variation and very shiny or dull skin reduce the score of radiance. A high score means that your skin has a healthy glow.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1194),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_care_tip_radiance", value = "<b>Care tips</b>\\nBalanced skincare requires a routine that leads to healthy-looking skin. In the case of using products to improve the look of your skin, more is not always better. In fact, using too many products can actually be detrimental to one's beauty regimen. A simple, less complicated, balanced approach to product use is better.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1195),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_expandable_firmness", value = "<b>What does it mean?</b>\\nSkin elasticity and firmness depend on the elastin and collagen content within the skin's dermal layer. Elastin is responsible for maintaining elasticity in the skin, while collagen keeps the skin structure in place and firm. As the skin gets older, it loses elastin fibres, collagen changes in structure and it finds it more difficult to retain water. This all reduces the elasticity of the skin, and fine lines and wrinkles can appear.\\n\\n<b>What do we measure?</b>\\nFirmness looks for signs of sagging/firm skin. A high score on firmness means that you have firm skin with no to little signs of skin sagging.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1196),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_care_tip_firmness", value = "<b>Care tips</b>\\nCertain habits and lifestyle will all take a toll on your skin, and you will notice that your skin changes as you get older. Some easy changes you can make to minimize premature aging. Sun has a huge impact on skin sagging. Look at your non-sun-exposed areas; they are usually firm up until a certain age. Spend a minute or two putting on SPF50 protection when you\u2019re going to be outside for a prolonged period, particularly in the summer, and you\u2019ll greatly reduce the damage done to your skin (e.g., losing firmness) by the sun\u2019s ultraviolet radiation.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1197),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_expandable_eye_bags", value = "<b>What does it mean?</b>\\nThe skin around your eyes is thin, delicate, can be prone to irritation and can easily show dark circles.\\n\\n<b>What do we measure?</b>\\nWe specifically looked at dark circles around your eyes. A high score means that you have no to little dark circles.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1198),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_care_tip_eye_bags", value = "<b>Care tips</b>\\nThe appearance of the eye area has a large impact on the overall appearance of the face. This area is often more delicate and requires a different type of care than the rest of the face. Some dark circles are transient and will recover. They are typically brought on by lifestyle, fatigue and lack of sleep. Other dark circles are more permanent and are brought on by aging.\\nDark circles under your eyes can be caused by a multitude of factors. Allergies, thinning of the skin, hyperpigmentation, genetics, lack of sleep can all contribute to dark circles forming under your eyes. Applying antioxidant-rich eye cream using a gentle massaging motion from your nose to the side of your face will stimulate blood flow to and lymph drainage from this area. A healthy lifestyle with adequate sleep and nutrition can also help to reduce them.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1199),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_expandable_skin_shine", value = "<b>What does it mean?</b>\\nA high oil level is nice for a good skin barrier and gives it a nice shine. Sebum contributes to the oiliness of the skin. Whilst usually spoken about negatively, sebum\u2019s purpose is to lubricate the skin and hair, as well as help the skin to maintain its barrier function. However, excessive sebum production can result in clogged pores.\\n\\n<b>What do we measure?</b>\\nTo detect skin shine, we looked at two areas of your skin:\\n\\u2022 The overall skin brightness, where we analysed how much your skin reflects light;\\n\\u2022 The sharp-edged reflection of light. \u2018Skin shine\u2019 looks for signs of oily skin.\\n\\nA high score means that you have a good amount of skin shine.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1200),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_care_tip_skin_shine", value = "<b>Care tips</b>\\nWhen it comes to getting the best out of your skin type, washing your face and neck twice a day is a great place to start. You should consider investing in a facewash developed specifically for your skin type. Gently wash your face with warm (but not hot) water in the morning to remove any build-up of sebum that has occurred overnight, and then again in the evening to clean off any excess oil that has accumulated during the day. The T-zone along the top of your brow and the bridge of your nose and the U-zone around your eyes may be particularly prone to oiliness, so be sure to cleanse these areas thoroughly.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1201),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_expandable_texture", value = "<b>What does it mean?</b>\\nWith \u2018texture\u2019 we mean skin that looks uneven and bumpy.\\n\\n<b>What do we measure?</b>\\nTo detect texture, we looked at all variations compared to a smooth and uniform surface. All kinds of skin roughness affect the score. Larger pores start to affect the score. A high score means good texture. A high score is considered desirable.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1202),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_care_tip_texture", value = "<b>Care tips</b>\\nBy exfoliating we can make our skin a little softer as exfoliation reveals the newer skin layers below and these new layers feel softer and look more radiant. For healthy-looking, soft-feeling skin, we recommend exfoliating once or twice a week.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1203),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_expandable_pigmentation_evenness", value = "<b>What does it mean?</b>\\nPigmentation evenness is the variation of skin colour induced by melanin. Melanin, produced by melanocytes in the skin's epidermis, defines a person's skin tone. It is generally defined by genetics.\\n\\n<b>What do we measure?</b>\\nFor \u2018Pigmentation evenness\u2019 we look at the variations in skin colour, signs of small to moderate uneven local differences in the skin appearance. The amount and severity of the skin colour variations are assessed together. A high score means good pigmentation evenness.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1204),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_skincare_care_tip_pigmentation_evenness", value = "<b>Care tips</b>\\nAdditional factors such as sun or free radical damage can influence melanin production. Increased production in one area can result in dark spots (uneven pigmentation).\\nThe main cause of dark spots is UV damage, but can be hormonal, a side-effect of medication, inflammation, or wound healing (such as after acne). For every skin, the use of sun protection (e.g., moisturiser with SPF) daily helps to minimise skin pigmentation. For warm sunny summer days, high SPF is recommended.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1205),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_progress", value = "Progress", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1206),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_overall_progress", value = "Overall progress", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1207),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_dashboard_msg_ongoing", value = "On-going", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1208),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_marketing_consent_help_text", value = "If you give us your consent, you will join our marketing initiatives and Philips will keep you up to date about our (including our brand licensee partners) products, services, promotions and events. Let us give you an overview of our marketing initiatives and explain to you how we will process your data.\\n\\n<b>Data you give us</b>\\n\\nData that you want to actively share with us such as: your name, date of birth or age, email address, physical address, country, gender, phone number, social media profile.\\n\\n<b>Data we get from your interactions with Philips</b>\\n\\nData about your interactions and usage of the Philips digital channels, such as social media, websites, emails, apps and connected products. This data may include: IP address, cookies, device information, communications you click on, location details, and websites you visit.\\n\\nPhilips will give you the opportunity to withdraw your consent at any time.", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1209),
    StringEntity(key = "lumea_privacy_control_text", value = "Privacy controls", isAndroid = true, isIos = true, rowNumber = 1210),
